  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "7185102e-8649-4c06-9009-19e36883d536",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Deneb Showcase from PowerShell\n\nThis experiment renders [Deneb Showcase](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase) Vega and Vega-Lite specifications in Verso notebook cells. Each chart cell loads a specification from the upstream repository, optionally replaces its data, and emits a self-contained Verso widget.\n\nThe examples are pinned to Deneb Showcase commit [\u0060eded225\u0060](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/commit/eded225be500aa9bdec51b72fbb94063e3a92af0) for repeatable notebook execution. Deneb Showcase is available under the [MIT License](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/blob/main/LICENSE)."
    },
    {
      "id": "91b17ccd-ced9-4645-a433-ad3774750979",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Helper commands\n\n\u0060helper.ps1\u0060 provides a small pipeline-oriented API:\n\n- \u0060Get-DenebShowcaseSpec\u0060 downloads a pinned Showcase specification.\n- \u0060Get-DenebShowcaseData\u0060 downloads a pinned companion JSON dataset.\n- \u0060Set-DenebSpecData\u0060 replaces one Vega-Lite source or multiple named Vega sources without mutating the original specification.\n- \u0060Set-DenebSpecSize\u0060 sets explicit top-level plot width and/or height on a copy; it does not move marks or change autosize/padding.\n- \u0060Show-Vega\u0060 and \u0060Show-VegaLite\u0060 render explicit grammar types.\n- \u0060Show-DenebShowcaseExample\u0060 is a convenience command that downloads, detects, and renders either type.\n\nThe generated HTML follows the same simple self-contained widget pattern now used by [PR #95](https://github.com/DataficationSDK/Verso/pull/95). It relies on the corrected Viewer behavior and does not include the old script-scope, shared-loader, or fixed-width workarounds."
    },
    {
      "id": "cf37f7c3-37f5-439c-a886-1525654c247b",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "#!import ./helper.ps1",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Imported helper.ps1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dc071946-4399-4ea4-bcb7-d61bed45b066",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vega-Lite: Calendar Heatmap \u2014 Irvine weather\n\nThe original [Calendar Heatmap](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/blob/main/Calendar%20Heatmap/Spec.json), with daily weather from [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/historical-weather-api).\n\n**Cell 1 \u2014 download.** Imports \u0060irvine-weather.ps1\u0060, loads the pinned template and downloads daily mean temperature (\u00B0C) and precipitation (mm) from **2023 through yesterday in America/Los_Angeles**. Re-run to refresh \u0060$irvineWeather\u0060. Default coordinates: Irvine, CA (33.6846, -117.8265). These are gridded historical reanalysis values, not a single weather station or future forecast. Returned grid coordinates and source URLs remain in the downloaded object.\n\n**Cell 2 \u2014 select.** Change \u0060$year\u0060 and \u0060$metric\u0060 (\u0060Temperature\u0060 or \u0060Precipitation\u0060), then run only that cell. The current year is incomplete; future days are absent. Missing readings stay null, not zero; the download cell reports coverage.\n\nThe original month/week/day layout remains intact. Both metrics use a blue-to-red gradient: low values are blue, the midpoint is light, and high values are red. The range adapts to the selected year and metric. Explicit ISO local-date parsing and full-year extraction preserve leap days and all weeks. Title, legend and tooltips identify the metric. Weather: Open-Meteo, CC BY 4.0. Dataviz: David Bacci."
    },
    {
      "id": "0e8d4a14-6e99-49e0-968a-0f0e6143daf7",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "#!import ./irvine-weather.ps1\n\n$calendarTemplate = Get-DenebShowcaseSpec \u0027Calendar Heatmap/Spec.json\u0027\n$irvineWeather = Get-IrvineDailyWeather -StartYear 2023\n\n$irvineWeather.Years |\n    Select-Object Year, Days, ThroughDate, MissingTemperature, MissingPrecipitation |\n    Format-Table",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Imported irvine-weather.ps1"
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/html",
          "content": "\u003Cstyle\u003E.verso-ps-result{--ps-bg:var(--vscode-editor-background,var(--verso-cell-output-background,#fff));--ps-fg:var(--vscode-editor-foreground,var(--verso-cell-output-foreground,#1e1e1e));--ps-border:var(--vscode-editorWidget-border,var(--verso-border-default,#e0e0e0));--ps-header-bg:var(--vscode-editorWidget-background,var(--verso-cell-background,#f5f5f5));--ps-hover:var(--vscode-list-hoverBackground,var(--verso-cell-hover-background,#f0f0f0));--ps-muted:var(--vscode-descriptionForeground,var(--verso-editor-line-number,#858585));font-family:var(--verso-code-output-font-family,monospace);font-size:13px;color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result table{border-collapse:collapse;width:auto;background:var(--ps-bg);color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result th{text-align:left;padding:6px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--ps-border);background:var(--ps-header-bg);font-weight:600;}.verso-ps-result td{padding:5px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ps-border);}.verso-ps-result tbody tr:hover{background:var(--ps-hover);}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-null{color:var(--ps-muted);font-style:italic;}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-footer{padding:6px 0;color:var(--ps-muted);font-size:12px;}\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-result\u0022\u003E\u003Ctable\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth\u003EYear\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EDays\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EThroughDate\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EMissingTemperature\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EMissingPrecipitation\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2023\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E365\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2023-12-31\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2024\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E366\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2024-12-31\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2025\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E365\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2025-12-31\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E241\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026-08-29\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-footer\u0022\u003E4 objects\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4017a2f0-1b60-4b7f-a916-456655d00721",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "$year = (Get-Date).Year\n$metric = \u0027Temperature\u0027 # Or \u0027Precipitation\u0027\n\n$calendarTemplate |\n    Set-WeatherCalendarYear -Weather $irvineWeather -Year $year -Metric $metric |\n    Show-VegaLite",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/x-verso-widget",
          "content": "\u003C!doctype html\u003E\n\u003Chtml\u003E\n\u003Chead\u003E\n    \u003Cmeta charset=\u0022utf-8\u0022\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega@6.3.1\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-lite@6.4.3\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-embed@7.1.0\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cstyle\u003E\n        html, body {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            background: var(--verso-cell-output-background, white);\n            color: var(--verso-cell-output-foreground, #1e1e1e);\n            font-family: var(--verso-ui-font-family, sans-serif);\n        }\n        #vis { width: 100%; overflow: auto; }\n        .error { padding: 12px; color: #c62828; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n    \u003C/style\u003E\n\u003C/head\u003E\n\u003Cbody\u003E\n    \u003Cdiv id=\u0022vis\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n    \u003Cscript\u003E\n        const binary = atob(\\u0022);\n        const bytes = Uint8Array.from(binary, character =\u003E character.charCodeAt(0));\n        const spec = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(bytes));\n\n        vegaEmbed(\u0022#vis\u0022, spec, {\n            mode: \u0022vega-lite\u0022,\n            renderer: \u0022svg\u0022,\n            actions: true\n        }).catch(error =\u003E {\n            document.body.innerHTML = \u0027\u003Cdiv class=\u0022error\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u0027;\n            document.querySelector(\u0022.error\u0022).textContent = error.stack || error.message;\n        });\n    \u003C/script\u003E\n\u003C/body\u003E\n\u003C/html\u003E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d6ddcf7b-4189-4b5a-abf9-2a38143e4c02",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vega: Mekko Chart \u2014 SIPRI military spending\n\nThe original [Marimekko specification](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/blob/main/Mekko%20Chart/Spec%20(Marimekko).json) by David Bacci, with refreshed [SIPRI military expenditure data](https://www.sipri.org/databases/milex). Region width represents its share of available spending; each country\u0027s height represents its share within that region. The spec combines Africa and the Middle East and groups small countries into Others.\n\n**Cell 1 \u2014 download once per kernel session.** Imports \u0060sipri-military-spending.ps1\u0060, loads the pinned spec, discovers SIPRI\u0027s latest official Excel download and reads all published, completed calendar years from **2023** into \u0060$sipriSpending\u0060. No Excel installation or extra PowerShell module is needed. Re-run to refresh.\n\n**Cell 2 \u2014 choose a year.** Edit \u0060$year\u0060 and run only that cell. SIPRI publishes **annual**, not quarterly, data, so there is no quarter parameter. The current release contains 2023\u20132025; there is no full-year 2026 figure yet. A fresh kernel needs the download cell first.\n\nData comes from the **Current US$** worksheet: millions of US dollars at current prices and exchange rates, by calendar year. The source can revise historical figures. The chart converts amounts to billions in its original labels. Country/entity names and regions are taken from SIPRI (including the separate European Union entry).\n\nMissing values are excluded, **not replaced by zero**; real zeros are retained. Blue/red source figures retain their \u0060Quality\u0060 flags (SIPRI estimate / highly uncertain) and footnote references in the loaded rows. Inspect \u0060$sipriSpending.Years | Where-Object Year -eq $year\u0060 for records, missing countries and totals. Shares refer to the available-country/entity sum, **not SIPRI\u0027s separate world/regional estimates**.\n\nOnly the spec\u0027s \u0060table\u0060 values, title and source credit change. Layout, grouping rules, colors and author attribution are preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "2f725315-3e8a-4ea8-a7e7-597cba796af5",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "#!import ./sipri-military-spending.ps1\n\n# Download the original template and all published years from 2023.\n$mekkoTemplate = Get-DenebShowcaseSpec \u0027Mekko Chart/Spec (Marimekko).json\u0027\n$sipriSpending = Get-SipriMilitarySpending -StartYear 2023\n\n# Available data and coverage; amounts remain in USD millions.\n$sipriSpending.Years |\n    Select-Object Year, EntityCount, MissingCount, ZeroCount, EstimateCount, UncertainCount |\n    Format-Table",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Imported sipri-military-spending.ps1"
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/html",
          "content": "\u003Cstyle\u003E.verso-ps-result{--ps-bg:var(--vscode-editor-background,var(--verso-cell-output-background,#fff));--ps-fg:var(--vscode-editor-foreground,var(--verso-cell-output-foreground,#1e1e1e));--ps-border:var(--vscode-editorWidget-border,var(--verso-border-default,#e0e0e0));--ps-header-bg:var(--vscode-editorWidget-background,var(--verso-cell-background,#f5f5f5));--ps-hover:var(--vscode-list-hoverBackground,var(--verso-cell-hover-background,#f0f0f0));--ps-muted:var(--vscode-descriptionForeground,var(--verso-editor-line-number,#858585));font-family:var(--verso-code-output-font-family,monospace);font-size:13px;color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result table{border-collapse:collapse;width:auto;background:var(--ps-bg);color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result th{text-align:left;padding:6px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--ps-border);background:var(--ps-header-bg);font-weight:600;}.verso-ps-result td{padding:5px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ps-border);}.verso-ps-result tbody tr:hover{background:var(--ps-hover);}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-null{color:var(--ps-muted);font-style:italic;}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-footer{padding:6px 0;color:var(--ps-muted);font-size:12px;}\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-result\u0022\u003E\u003Ctable\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth\u003EYear\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EEntityCount\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EMissingCount\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EZeroCount\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EEstimateCount\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EUncertainCount\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2023\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E155\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E14\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E3\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E11\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E4\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2024\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E154\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E15\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E3\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E11\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E3\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2025\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E152\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E17\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E3\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E11\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-footer\u0022\u003E3 objects\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ba80f67b-8ab4-469e-85c2-5210938fce2f",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "$year = 2025\n\n$mekkoTemplate |\n    Set-SipriMekkoYear -Spending $sipriSpending -Year $year |\n    Show-Vega -Renderer canvas",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/x-verso-widget",
          "content": "\u003C!doctype html\u003E\n\u003Chtml\u003E\n\u003Chead\u003E\n    \u003Cmeta charset=\u0022utf-8\u0022\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega@6.3.1\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-lite@6.4.3\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-embed@7.1.0\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cstyle\u003E\n        html, body {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            background: var(--verso-cell-output-background, white);\n            color: var(--verso-cell-output-foreground, #1e1e1e);\n            font-family: var(--verso-ui-font-family, sans-serif);\n        }\n        #vis { width: 100%; overflow: auto; }\n        .error { padding: 12px; color: #c62828; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n    \u003C/style\u003E\n\u003C/head\u003E\n\u003Cbody\u003E\n    \u003Cdiv id=\u0022vis\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n    \u003Cscript\u003E\n        const binary = atob(\\\u0022);\n        const bytes = Uint8Array.from(binary, character =\u003E character.charCodeAt(0));\n        const spec = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(bytes));\n\n        vegaEmbed(\u0022#vis\u0022, spec, {\n            mode: \u0022vega\u0022,\n            renderer: \u0022canvas\u0022,\n            actions: true\n        }).catch(error =\u003E {\n            document.body.innerHTML = \u0027\u003Cdiv class=\u0022error\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u0027;\n            document.querySelector(\u0022.error\u0022).textContent = error.stack || error.message;\n        });\n    \u003C/script\u003E\n\u003C/body\u003E\n\u003C/html\u003E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f5d05e24-ed51-455d-8a22-e1919a0ac915",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vega: Sankey Chart \u2014 Microsoft fiscal quarters\n\nThe original [David Bacci Sankey specification](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/blob/main/Sankey%20Chart/Spec.json), with official [Microsoft Investor Relations](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/Investor/earnings) data.\n\n**Cell 1 \u2014 download once per kernel session.** Loads the pinned spec and every available completed quarter from **FY2023**, keeping the result in \u0060$microsoftFinancials\u0060. It prints the available periods and any HTTP 404 gaps. Other download/parsing errors stop execution; no estimates or sample-data fallback. Re-run to refresh the data.\n\n**Cell 2 \u2014 choose a period.** Edit \u0060$year\u0060 and \u0060$quarter\u0060, then run only that cell. Selection and spec binding need no further financial-data downloads. A fresh kernel must run the download cell first.\n\nYears are **Microsoft fiscal years**, not calendar years: Q1 = Jul\u2013Sep of the preceding year; Q2 = Oct\u2013Dec; Q3 = Jan\u2013Mar; Q4 = Apr\u2013Jun. FY2023 therefore starts in July 2022.\n\nThe adapter in \u0060microsoft-financials.ps1\u0060 uses the current-period column, in USD millions. Where Q4 tables contain annual amounts, it subtracts Q3 year-to-date values. Records retain source URLs and derived-field metadata. Values are **as reported**; segment reorganizations (including FY2025) mean historical segment amounts are not a restated comparable series.\n\nOnly the spec\u0027s \u0060input\u0060 data, title and source credit change. Its drawing logic and dimensions remain original. Revenue starts with the three reported segments, not estimated product-level allocations. Other income/expense and pretax income are included so the flows balance. The chart converts millions to **USD billions**."
    },
    {
      "id": "bab99739-a80e-4d3f-81ac-0ce43a214126",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "#!import ./microsoft-financials.ps1\n\n# Download once. All periods remain in this kernel session.\n$sankeyTemplate = Get-DenebShowcaseSpec \u0027Sankey Chart/Spec.json\u0027\n$microsoftFinancials = Get-MicrosoftQuarterlyFinancials -StartYear 2023\n\n# Microsoft fiscal periods; financial amounts below are USD millions.\n$microsoftFinancials.Quarters |\n    Select-Object Year, Quarter, PeriodEnd, Revenue, NetIncome |\n    Format-Table",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Imported microsoft-financials.ps1"
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "WARNING: FY2026 Q4 is unavailable at Microsoft IR (HTTP 404); no data substituted."
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/html",
          "content": "\u003Cstyle\u003E.verso-ps-result{--ps-bg:var(--vscode-editor-background,var(--verso-cell-output-background,#fff));--ps-fg:var(--vscode-editor-foreground,var(--verso-cell-output-foreground,#1e1e1e));--ps-border:var(--vscode-editorWidget-border,var(--verso-border-default,#e0e0e0));--ps-header-bg:var(--vscode-editorWidget-background,var(--verso-cell-background,#f5f5f5));--ps-hover:var(--vscode-list-hoverBackground,var(--verso-cell-hover-background,#f0f0f0));--ps-muted:var(--vscode-descriptionForeground,var(--verso-editor-line-number,#858585));font-family:var(--verso-code-output-font-family,monospace);font-size:13px;color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result table{border-collapse:collapse;width:auto;background:var(--ps-bg);color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result th{text-align:left;padding:6px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--ps-border);background:var(--ps-header-bg);font-weight:600;}.verso-ps-result td{padding:5px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ps-border);}.verso-ps-result tbody tr:hover{background:var(--ps-hover);}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-null{color:var(--ps-muted);font-style:italic;}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-footer{padding:6px 0;color:var(--ps-muted);font-size:12px;}\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-result\u0022\u003E\u003Ctable\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth\u003EYear\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EQuarter\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EPeriodEnd\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003ERevenue\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003ENetIncome\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2023\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E1\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2022-09-30\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E50122.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E17556.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2023\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2022-12-31\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E52747.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E16425.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2023\u