    {
      "id": "2ee69c25-2851-4ce6-af5f-1f7bbd179af9",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vega: Bank Failure Bubble Chart \u2014 FDIC\n\nThe original [Bank Failure Bubble Chart (Absolute)](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/blob/main/Bank%20Failure%20Bubble%20Chart/Spec%20(Absolute).json) with refreshed [FDIC BankFind data](https://banks.data.fdic.gov/explore/failures).\n\n**Cell 1 \u2014 download.** Imports \u0060fdic-bank-failures.ps1\u0060, loads the pinned spec and downloads all failures from **2001 through today** into \u0060$bankFailures\u0060. Only \u0060RESTYPE=FAILURE\u0060, not assistance transactions. Pagination checks prevent silently truncated or duplicated data. Re-run to refresh.\n\n**Cell 2 \u2014 select years.** Edit \u0060$startYear\u0060 and \u0060$endYear\u0060, then run only that cell. Both must be within downloaded coverage. A period with no failures produces an explicit message, not fabricated bubbles.\n\nBubble values are **nominal assets from the last financial report filed before failure**, not FDIC losses or insured deposits. FDIC\u0027s \u0060QBFASSET\u0060 is in thousands of USD and is multiplied by 1,000 for the original spec. Values can differ from press-release estimates in the old Showcase dataset. No inflation adjustment is applied.\n\nDate-axis bounds and title follow the selection. The original force animation, drawing logic, dimensions, colors and author credit remain intact. Let the animation settle; hover bubbles for bank, date and assets."
    },
    {
      "id": "f7bc8cb3-d7e6-4565-97e9-41f7b007ec38",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "#!import ./fdic-bank-failures.ps1\n\n$bankFailureTemplate = Get-DenebShowcaseSpec \u0027Bank Failure Bubble Chart/Spec (Absolute).json\u0027\n$bankFailures = Get-FdicBankFailures -StartYear 2001\n\n$bankFailures.Years |\n    Select-Object Year, Failures, AssetsBillions |\n    Format-Table",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Imported fdic-bank-failures.ps1"
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/html",
          "content": "\u003Cstyle\u003E.verso-ps-result{--ps-bg:var(--vscode-editor-background,var(--verso-cell-output-background,#fff));--ps-fg:var(--vscode-editor-foreground,var(--verso-cell-output-foreground,#1e1e1e));--ps-border:var(--vscode-editorWidget-border,var(--verso-border-default,#e0e0e0));--ps-header-bg:var(--vscode-editorWidget-background,var(--verso-cell-background,#f5f5f5));--ps-hover:var(--vscode-list-hoverBackground,var(--verso-cell-hover-background,#f0f0f0));--ps-muted:var(--vscode-descriptionForeground,var(--verso-editor-line-number,#858585));font-family:var(--verso-code-output-font-family,monospace);font-size:13px;color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result table{border-collapse:collapse;width:auto;background:var(--ps-bg);color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result th{text-align:left;padding:6px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--ps-border);background:var(--ps-header-bg);font-weight:600;}.verso-ps-result td{padding:5px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ps-border);}.verso-ps-result tbody tr:hover{background:var(--ps-hover);}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-null{color:var(--ps-muted);font-style:italic;}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-footer{padding:6px 0;color:var(--ps-muted);font-size:12px;}\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-result\u0022\u003E\u003Ctable\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth\u003EYear\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EFailures\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EAssetsBillions\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2001\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E4\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E1.822\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2002\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E11\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2.873\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2003\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E3\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0.947\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2004\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E4\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E0.170\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u0