    {
      "id": "6c5f535b-65a3-410a-835d-2280b6dbe0d5",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vega: Population Bar Chart Race \u2014 World Bank\n\nThe original [Population Bar Chart Race](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/tree/main/Population%20Bar%20Chart%20Race), with annual World Bank WDI population (SP.POP.TOTL).\n\n**Download cell:** loads the pinned template and all published completed years from 1960. Pagination, duplicates and source revision are checked. No API key. The latest available year is discovered, not assumed to be the current year.\n\n**Display cell:** choose start/end years, Top N, World Bank region ID (or All), and seconds per year. Click to play/pause; use the original restart control at bottom right. It opens paused. Only economies with complete annual series throughout the chosen period participate; exclusions are reported in the title and spec metadata. Missing values and forecasts are not converted to zeros. Shorten the period to include more economies.\n\nColors use current World Bank regions, not historical boundaries. Countries/economies include territories; regional aggregates are excluded. The displayed World number is the separately published WLD total, not the sum of Top N or filtered economies. Intermediate animation frames are interpolation, not extra observations. Source: World Bank WDI; dataviz: David Bacci."
    },
    {
      "id": "88e904e4-6ff2-43a1-b7ea-5c89623625a3",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "#!import ./world-bank-population.ps1\n\n$populationTemplate = Get-DenebShowcaseSpec \u0027Population Bar Chart Race/Spec.json\u0027\n$worldPopulation = Get-WorldBankPopulation -StartYear 1960\n\n$worldPopulation.Years | Select-Object -Last 6 |\n    Format-Table Year, AvailableEconomies, WorldPopulation\n\n$worldPopulation.Rows | Where-Object Code -ne \u0027WLD\u0027 |\n    Select-Object RegionId, Continent -Unique | Format-Table",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Imported world-bank-population.ps1"
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/html",
          "content": "\u003Cstyle\u003E.verso-ps-result{--ps-bg:var(--vscode-editor-background,var(--verso-cell-output-background,#fff));--ps-fg:var(--vscode-editor-foreground,var(--verso-cell-output-foreground,#1e1e1e));--ps-border:var(--vscode-editorWidget-border,var(--verso-border-default,#e0e0e0));--ps-header-bg:var(--vscode-editorWidget-background,var(--verso-cell-background,#f5f5f5));--ps-hover:var(--vscode-list-hoverBackground,var(--verso-cell-hover-background,#f0f0f0));--ps-muted:var(--vscode-descriptionForeground,var(--verso-editor-line-number,#858585));font-family:var(--verso-code-output-font-family,monospace);font-size:13px;color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result table{border-collapse:collapse;width:auto;background:var(--ps-bg);color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result th{text-align:left;padding:6px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--ps-border);background:var(--ps-header-bg);font-weight:600;}.verso-ps-result td{padding:5px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ps-border);}.verso-ps-result tbody tr:hover{background:var(--ps-hover);}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-null{color:var(--ps-muted);font-style:italic;}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-footer{padding:6px 0;color:var(--ps-muted);font-size:12px;}\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-result\u0022\u003E\u003Ctable\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth\u003EYear\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EAvailableEconomies\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EWorldPopulation\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2020\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E217\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E7853863139.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2021\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E217\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E7919567995.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2022\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E217\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E7988550201.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2023\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E217\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8062923417.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2024\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E217\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8140897523.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2025\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E217\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8215424893.000\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ERegi\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EonId Continent\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E----\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E---- ---------\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EMEA\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EMiddle East, N\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eorth Africa, Afghanistan \u0026amp; Pakistan\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EECS\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEurope \u0026amp; Centr\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eal Asia\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEAS\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEast Asia \u0026amp; Pa\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ecific\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ESSF\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ESub-Saharan Af\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Erica\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ELCN\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ELatin America\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u0026amp; Caribbean\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ESAS\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ESouth Asia\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENAC\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENorth America\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-footer\u0022\u003E15 objects\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8b736410-dea7-4d87-b471-6cd0878f651b",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "$startYear = 1960\n$endYear = $worldPopulation.LatestYear\n$topN = 12\n$region = \u0027All\u0027 # Or a RegionId listed by the download cell, e.g. ECS.\n$secondsPerYear = 0.6\n\n$populationTemplate |\n    Set-WorldBankPopulationRace -Population $worldPopulation -StartYear $startYear -EndYear $endYear \u0060\n        -TopN $topN -Region $region -SecondsPerYear $secondsPerYear |\n    Show-Vega -Renderer canvas",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/x-verso-widget",
          "content": "\u003C!doctype html\u003E\n\u003Chtml\u003E\n\u003Chead\u003E\n    \u003Cmeta charset=\u0022utf-8\u0022\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega@6.3.1\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-lite@6.4.3\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-embed@7.1.0\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cstyle\u003E\n        html, body {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            background: var(--verso-cell-output-background, white);\n            color: var(--verso-cell-output-foreground, #1e1e1e);\n            font-family: var(--verso-ui-font-family, sans-serif);\n        }\n        #vis { width: 100%; overflow: auto; }\n        .error { padding: 12px; color: #c62828; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n    \u003C/style\u003E\n\u003C/head\u003E\n\u003Cbody\u003E\n    \u003Cdiv id=\u0022vis\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n    \u003Cscript\u003E\n        const binary = atob(\\u0022);\n        const bytes = Uint8Array.from(binary, character =\u003E character.charCodeAt(0));\n        const spec = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(bytes));\n\n        vegaEmbed(\u0022#vis\u0022, spec, {\n            mode: \u0022vega\u0022,\n            renderer: \u0022canvas\u0022,\n            actions: true\n        }).catch(error =\u003E {\n            document.body.innerHTML = \u0027\u003Cdiv class=\u0022error\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u0027;\n            document.querySelector(\u0022.error\u0022).textContent = error.stack || error.message;\n        });\n    \u003C/script\u003E\n\u003C/body\u003E\n\u003C/html\u003E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "84bf990e-00be-47f0-bb73-7e4153e50718",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vega: Parallel Coordinates \u2014 NASA exoplanets\n\nThe original [Parallel Coordinates Chart](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/tree/main/Parallel%20Coordinates%20Chart), with the current [NASA Exoplanet Archive composite catalogue](https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/docs/API_PS_columns.html) (PSCompPars, one row per planet).\n\n**Download cell:** loads the pinned template and catalogue, retaining missing values and limit flags. No API key. The record cap fails visibly instead of silently truncating. The summary reports coverage.\n\n**Display cell:** choose discovery year, maximum radius in Earth radii, distance in parsecs, discovery method, and maximum lines. Newest discovery years first, then planet name; the title reports shown versus matching records. This is a filtered selection, not a representative sample.\n\nFive axes: radius, orbital period (days), distance (pc), stellar effective temperature (K), discovery year. The first three use logarithmic scales. Drag an axis to select a range, drag titles to reorder axes, double-click to reset. Hover a line for its planet and source values.\n\nOnly complete, positive values with zero limit flags and noncontroversial catalogue status are plotted; no imputation. Composite values may be derived and may combine different publications. Stellar temperature is NOT planetary temperature. This is not a habitability score. Source: NASA Exoplanet Archive; dataviz: David Bacci."
    },
    {
      "id": "df030260-52da-4c92-9fe6-b6ef10efb2ab",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "#!import ./nasa-exoplanets.ps1\n\n$exoplanetTemplate = Get-DenebShowcaseSpec \u0027Parallel Coordinates Chart/Spec.json\u0027\n$exoplanetCatalogue = Get-NasaExoplanets\n\n$exoplanetCatalogue.Summary | Format-List\n$exoplanetCatalogue.Rows | Group-Object Method |\n    Sort-Object Count -Descending | Format-Table Name, Count",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Imported nasa-exoplanets.ps1"
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/html",
          "content": "\u003Cstyle\u003E.verso-ps-result{--ps-bg:var(--vscode-editor-background,var(--verso-cell-output-background,#fff));--ps-fg:var(--vscode-editor-foreground,var(--verso-cell-output-foreground,#1e1e1e));font-family:var(--verso-code-output-font-family,monospace);font-size:13px;color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-pre{margin:0;white-space:pre;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:1.4;}\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-result\u0022\u003E\u003Cpre class=\u0022verso-ps-pre\u0022\u003EPlanets                  : 6354\nMissingOrNonPositive     : 433\nWithLimitsOrUnknownFlags : 423\nEligible                 : 5865\nName                          Count\n----                          -----\nTransit                        4688\nRadial Velocity                1200\nMicrolensing                    283\nImaging                          98\nTransit Timing Variations        42\nEclipse Timing Variations        17\nOrbital Brightness Modulation     9\nPulsar Timing                     8\nAstrometry                        6\nPulsation Timing Variations       2\nDisk Kinematics                   1\u003C/pre\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3c1bd83f-b4f1-471b-8f94-0274806ceeb2",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "$minDiscoveryYear = 2020\n$maxRadiusEarth = 4\n$maxDistancePc = 200\n$method = \u0027All\u0027 # Or a discovery method listed above, e.g. Transit.\n$maxPlanets = 250\n\n$exoplanetTemplate |\n    Set-NasaExoplanetCoordinates -Catalogue $exoplanetCatalogue -MinDiscoveryYear $minDiscoveryYear \u0060\n        -MaxRadiusEarth $maxRadiusEarth -MaxDistancePc $maxDistancePc -Method $method -MaxPlanets $maxPlanets |\n    Show-Vega -Renderer canvas",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/x-verso-widget",
          "content": "\u003C!doctype html\u003E\n\u003Chtml\u003E\n\u003Chead\u003E\n    \u003Cmeta charset=\u0022utf-8\u0022\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega@6.3.1\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-lite@6.4.3\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cscript src=\u0022https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-embed@7.1.0\u0022\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\n    \u003Cstyle\u003E\n        html, body {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            background: var(--verso-cell-output-background, white);\n            color: var(--verso-cell-output-foreground, #1e1e1e);\n            font-family: var(--verso-ui-font-family, sans-serif);\n        }\n        #vis { width: 100%; overflow: auto; }\n        .error { padding: 12px; color: #c62828; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n    \u003C/style\u003E\n\u003C/head\u003E\n\u003Cbody\u003E\n    \u003Cdiv id=\u0022vis\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n    \u003Cscript\u003E\n        const binary = atob(\\u002BIHdpbmRvdzpwb2ludGVybW92ZSxbQGJydXNoOnBvaW50ZXJkb3duLCB3aW5kb3c6cG9pbnRlcnVwXSA\\u002BIHdpbmRvdzpwb2ludGVybW92ZSEiLCJ1cGRhdGUiOiInZ3JhYicifSx7ImV2ZW50cyI6IkBheGlzRG9tYWluczpwb2ludGVyb3ZlcixbQGF4aXNEb21haW5zOnBvaW50ZXJkb3duLCB3aW5kb3c6cG9pbnRlcnVwXSA\u002BIHdpbmRvdzpwb2ludGVybW92ZSEiLCJ1cGRhdGUiOiIncm93LXJlc2l6ZScifSx7ImV2ZW50cyI6IkBicnVzaDpwb2ludGVyb3ZlcixbQGJydXNoOnBvaW50ZXJkb3duLCB3aW5kb3c6cG9pbnRlcnVwXSA\\\u0022);\n        const bytes = Uint8Array.from(binary, character =\u003E character.charCodeAt(0));\n        const spec = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(bytes));\n\n        vegaEmbed(\u0022#vis\u0022, spec, {\n            mode: \u0022vega\u0022,\n            renderer: \u0022canvas\u0022,\n            actions: true\n        }).catch(error =\u003E {\n            document.body.innerHTML = \u0027\u003Cdiv class=\u0022error\u0022\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u0027;\n            document.querySelector(\u0022.error\u0022).textContent = error.stack || error.message;\n        });\n    \u003C/script\u003E\n\u003C/body\u003E\n\u003C/html\u003E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "48a1b478-1d82-4a16-9856-ab3c3333f4ef",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vega-Lite: Waffle Charts \u2014 Great Britain electricity\n\nThe original [faceted Waffle Charts](https://github.com/PBI-David/Deneb-Showcase/tree/main/Waffle%20Charts), with generation-mix percentages from the [NESO Carbon Intensity API](https://carbon-intensity.github.io/api-definitions/#generation-mix). This covers the Great Britain electricity system, including imports, not all UK electricity and not carbon intensity.\n\n**Download cell:** fetches the last 48 hours of completed UTC half hours. Re-run to refresh. Duplicate intervals, missing/unknown fuels, invalid percentages and inconsistent totals fail visibly; missing intervals are reported, never filled with zeros. API values may be revised. No API key.\n\n**Display cell:** select an exact FromUtc from the downloaded intervals; the default is the latest available completed interval. Changing the selection makes no network request. UTC timestamps avoid ambiguity around British daylight-saving changes.\n\nEach source has its own 100-dot panel, arranged in three columns. Labels and tooltips retain the API percentage; filled dots round it to the nearest integer percentage point. These are nine independent percentage panels, not one shared 100-dot allocation; rounded dots need not add up to 100. Source percentages are never renormalized. Small nonzero shares can have no filled dots but remain visible in the numeric labels. Real zeros are retained.\n\nThe original grid transforms and layered marks are preserved; the car-count aggregation is replaced by API percentages. Source: NESO Carbon Intensity API, CC BY 4.0. Dataviz: David Bacci."
    },
    {
      "id": "c216b5ba-1c87-42e4-b5d2-8070376080a6",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "#!import ./gb-electricity.ps1\n\n$electricityTemplate = Get-DenebShowcaseSpec \u0027Waffle Charts/Spec.json\u0027\n$gbGeneration = Get-GbGenerationMix -Hours 48\n\nWrite-Host \u0022Loaded $($gbGeneration.Intervals.Count) / $($gbGeneration.ExpectedIntervals) completed intervals; missing: $($gbGeneration.MissingFromUtc.Count).\u0022\n$gbGeneration.Intervals |\n    Select-Object -Last 12 -Property FromUtc, ToUtc, TotalPercent",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Imported gb-electricity.ps1"
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "Loaded 96 / 96 completed intervals; missing: 0."
        },
        {
          "mimeType": "text/html",
          "content": "\u003Cstyle\u003E.verso-ps-result{--ps-bg:var(--vscode-editor-background,var(--verso-cell-output-background,#fff));--ps-fg:var(--vscode-editor-foreground,var(--verso-cell-output-foreground,#1e1e1e));--ps-border:var(--vscode-editorWidget-border,var(--verso-border-default,#e0e0e0));--ps-header-bg:var(--vscode-editorWidget-background,var(--verso-cell-background,#f5f5f5));--ps-hover:var(--vscode-list-hoverBackground,var(--verso-cell-hover-background,#f0f0f0));--ps-muted:var(--vscode-descriptionForeground,var(--verso-editor-line-number,#858585));font-family:var(--verso-code-output-font-family,monospace);font-size:13px;color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result table{border-collapse:collapse;width:auto;background:var(--ps-bg);color:var(--ps-fg);}.verso-ps-result th{text-align:left;padding:6px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--ps-border);background:var(--ps-header-bg);font-weight:600;}.verso-ps-result td{padding:5px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ps-border);}.verso-ps-result tbody tr:hover{background:var(--ps-hover);}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-null{color:var(--ps-muted);font-style:italic;}.verso-ps-result .verso-ps-footer{padding:6px 0;color:var(--ps-muted);font-size:12px;}\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022verso-ps-result\u0022\u003E\u003Ctable\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth\u003EFromUtc\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EToUtc\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003ETotalPercent\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026-08-31T12:00Z\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026-08-31T12:30Z\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E100\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026-08-31T12:30Z\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026-08-31T13:00Z\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E99.9\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026-08-31T13:00Z\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026-08-31T13:30Z\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E100\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E2026-08-31T13:30Z\u003C/td\u00